 HISTORY                                                          7250 1451
 -------                                                          7250 1451
    This library was produced by the Low Energy Interaction       7250 1451
    Physics (LEIP) group at North Carolina State University, USA. 7250 1451
    The thermal scattering law data for Oxygen in Plutonium       7250 1451
    Dioxide was developed using ab initio lattice dynamics        7250 1451
    (AILD)[1,2]. The PuO2 (space group 225) ground state          7250 1451
    structure is approximated in VASP with AFM-1K magnetic order  7250 1451
    and spin-orbit-coupling. Semi-itinerant Pu 5f electrons,      7250 1451
    hybridized with O 2p electrons, are modelled with an          7250 1451
    effective Hubbard term of 5 eV. A 500 eV plane-wave cutoff,   7250 1451
    9x9x9 k-mesh, GGA-PBEsol exhchange-correlations and Gaussian  7250 1451
    smearing ensure converged electronic structure. Phonon DOS    7250 1451
    were generated using a 2x2x2 supercell in PHONON using the    7250 1451
    dynamical-matrix method. Twelve temperatures are available in 7250 1451
    this library. The Full Law Analysis Scattering System Hub     7250 1451
    (FLASSH) system was used to produce File 7 MT = 2, 4 data for 7250 1451
    Oxygen in PuO2 [3] reflecting natural Oxygen abundances [5],  7250 1451
    100% Pu-239 and experimental lattice constants [6]. MAT=7250  7250 1451
    and ZA=7350 are used for natural Oxygen in PuO2.              7250 1451
